  /apis/{vendor}/{name}/{version}/overlays/{overlay_id}:confirm:
    description: '`POST`: Confirm an overlay and apply it to the served spec.'
    post:
      description: |-
        Apply a pending overlay, producing a new current revision of the API.

        The base spec is re-imported with the overlay applied and the result is
        promoted to the API's current revision, so it is what the API now serves.
        The overlay becomes `confirmed`. Confirming an already-applied overlay is
        a no-op that returns it unchanged; a deprecated overlay is refused with
        409 (`overlay_conflict`), and an overlay whose actions cannot be applied
        with 409 (`overlay_apply_conflict`).

        Requires `overlays:confirm` (implied by `org:admin`): contributors submit
        overlays with `apis:write`, and an operator reviews and confirms them.
        Agents cannot grant themselves this permission. Returns the overlay.
      operationId: confirmOverlay
      parameters:
      - description: Vendor of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API vendor domain
            value: stripe.com
        in: path
        name: vendor
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Vendor of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe.com
          title: Vendor
          type: string
      - description: Name of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API name
            value: stripe
        in: path
        name: name
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Name of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe
          title: Name
          type: string
      - description: Version of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API version
            value: '2024-04-10'
        in: path
        name: version
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Version of the API.
          examples:
          - '2024-04-10'
          title: Version
          type: string
      - description: ID of the overlay.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: Overlay ID
            value: ovr_6968b398ae1c9a6e2fe6520a
        in: path
        name: overlay_id
        required: true
        schema:
          description: ID of the overlay.
          examples:
          - ovr_6968b398ae1c9a6e2fe6520a
          title: Overlay Id
          type: string
      requestBody:
        content:
          application/json:
            example: *id208
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/OverlayConfirmRequest'
        description: Payload for confirming an overlay.
        required: true
      responses:
        '200':
          content:
            application/json:
              example: *id206
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OverlayResponse'
          description: Successful Response
        '400':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id169
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Bad Request
        '401':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id170
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unauthorized
        '403':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id171
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Forbidden
        '422':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id172
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unprocessable Entity
        '500':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id166
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Internal Server Error
        '503':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id173
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Service Unavailable
        default:
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id166
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unexpected error, as RFC 9457 Problem Details.
      security:
      - BearerAuth: []
      - OAuth2: []
      summary: Confirm an overlay and apply it to the served spec
      tags:
      - Overlays
    summary: Confirm an overlay and apply it to the served spec
  /apis/{vendor}/{name}/{version}/overlays/{overlay_id}:rollback:
    description: '`POST`: Roll back a confirmed overlay.'
    post:
      description: |-
        Undo a confirmed overlay by restoring the revision it replaced.

        The overlay's revision is archived and the revision it superseded becomes
        the API's current revision again, so the served spec reverts, and the
        overlay is marked `deprecated`. Requires `overlays:confirm`, like
        confirming.

        Preconditions: the overlay is `confirmed`, its revision is still the
        live one, and the revision it replaced is still restorable. Otherwise
        nothing changes and 409 is returned: `overlay_conflict`,
        `overlay_rollback_target_missing`, or `host_owned_by_other_vendor` when
        another vendor's live API now serves one of the restored revision's
        hosts. Returns 204.
      operationId: rollbackOverlay
      parameters:
      - description: Vendor of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API vendor domain
            value: stripe.com
        in: path
        name: vendor
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Vendor of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe.com
          title: Vendor
          type: string
      - description: Name of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API name
            value: stripe
        in: path
        name: name
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Name of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe
          title: Name
          type: string
      - description: Version of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API version
            value: '2024-04-10'
        in: path
        name: version
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Version of the API.
          examples:
          - '2024-04-10'
          title: Version
          type: string
      - description: ID of the overlay.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: Overlay ID
            value: ovr_6968b398ae1c9a6e2fe6520a
        in: path
        name: overlay_id
        required: true
        schema:
          description: ID of the overlay.
          examples:
          - ovr_6968b398ae1c9a6e2fe6520a
          title: Overlay Id
          type: string
      responses:
        '204':
          description: Successful Response
        '400':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id169
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Bad Request
        '401':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id170
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unauthorized
        '403':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id171
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Forbidden
        '422':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id172
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unprocessable Entity
        '500':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id166
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Internal Server Error
        '503':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id173
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Service Unavailable
        default:
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id166
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unexpected error, as RFC 9457 Problem Details.
      security:
      - BearerAuth: []
      - OAuth2: []
      summary: Roll back a confirmed overlay
      tags:
      - Overlays
    summary: Roll back a confirmed overlay
  /apis/{vendor}/{name}/{version}/revisions:
    description: '`GET`: List an API''s revisions.'
    get:
      description: |-
        List every revision imported for an API, newest first.

        Each revision gives its `state` (`draft`, `published`, `imported` or
        `archived`), whether it `is_current` (the one served), its source, spec
        digest, operation count and lifecycle timestamps, plus links to the
        actions valid in its state. Repeat `state` to filter by several states.
        Results are cursor-paginated: pass `next_cursor` as `cursor` while
        `has_more` is true. Fetch one revision with
        `GET /apis/{vendor}/{name}/{version}/revisions/{revision_id}`.
      operationId: listApiRevisions
      parameters:
      - description: Vendor of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API vendor domain
            value: stripe.com
        in: path
        name: vendor
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Vendor of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe.com
          title: Vendor
          type: string
      - description: Name of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API name
            value: stripe
        in: path
        name: name
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Name of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe
          title: Name
          type: string
      - description: Version of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API version
            value: '2024-04-10'
        in: path
        name: version
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Version of the API.
          examples:
          - '2024-04-10'
          title: Version
          type: string
      - description: Only return revisions in these states; repeat to match several.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: Example query value for `state`
            value: &id209
            - published
        in: query
        name: state
        required: false
        schema:
          anyOf:
          - examples:
            - *id209
            items:
              examples:
              - published
              type: string
            type: array
          - type: 'null'
          description: Only return revisions in these states; repeat to match several.
          examples:
          - *id209
          title: State
      - description: Opaque cursor from a previous page's `next_cursor`; omit for the first page.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: Opaque cursor from a previous page
            value: eyJ0IjogIjIwMjYtMDEtMTVUMDk6MzA6MDArMDA6MDAiLCAiaWQiOiAiM2YyYjhjMWUtN2Q0YS00ZTliLWE2YzUtMWQyZTNmNGE1YjZjIn0=
        in: query
        name: cursor
        required: false
        schema:
          anyOf:
          - examples:
            - eyJ0IjogIjIwMjYtMDEtMTVUMDk6MzA6MDArMDA6MDAiLCAiaWQiOiAiM2YyYjhjMWUtN2Q0YS00ZTliLWE2YzUtMWQyZTNmNGE1YjZjIn0=
            type: string
          - type: 'null'
          description: Opaque cursor from a previous page's `next_cursor`; omit for the first page.
          examples:
          - eyJ0IjogIjIwMjYtMDEtMTVUMDk6MzA6MDArMDA6MDAiLCAiaWQiOiAiM2YyYjhjMWUtN2Q0YS00ZTliLWE2YzUtMWQyZTNmNGE1YjZjIn0=
          title: Cursor
      - description: Maximum number of revisions to return (1-200).
        examples:
          example:
            summary: Example query value for `limit`
            value: 25
        in: query
        name: limit
        required: false
        schema:
          default: 50
          description: Maximum number of revisions to return (1-200).
          examples:
          - 25
          maximum: 200
          minimum: 1
          title: Limit
          type: integer
      responses:
        '200':
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: {}
          description: Successful Response
        '400':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id169
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Bad Request
        '401':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id170
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unauthorized
        '403':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id171
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Forbidden
        '422':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id172
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unprocessable Entity
        '500':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id166
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Internal Server Error
        '503':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id173
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Service Unavailable
        default:
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id166
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Unexpected error, as RFC 9457 Problem Details.
      security:
      - BearerAuth: []
      - OAuth2: []
      summary: List an API's revisions
      tags:
      - APIs
    summary: List an API's revisions
  /apis/{vendor}/{name}/{version}/revisions/{revision_id}:
    delete:
      description: |-
        Permanently delete an archived revision.

        Only an `archived` revision can be deleted — archive it first; any other
        state is refused with 409 (`revision_state_conflict`). Deletion cannot
        be undone. Requires `apis:write`. Returns 204.
      operationId: deleteRevision
      parameters:
      - description: Vendor of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API vendor domain
            value: stripe.com
        in: path
        name: vendor
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Vendor of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe.com
          title: Vendor
          type: string
      - description: Name of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API name
            value: stripe
        in: path
        name: name
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Name of the API.
          examples:
          - stripe
          title: Name
          type: string
      - description: Version of the API.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: API version
            value: '2024-04-10'
        in: path
        name: version
        required: true
        schema:
          description: Version of the API.
          examples:
          - '2024-04-10'
          title: Version
          type: string
      - description: ID of the API revision.
        examples:
          example:
            summary: Revision ID (UUID)
            value: 3f2b8c1e-7d4a-4e9b-a6c5-1d2e3f4a5b6c
        in: path
        name: revision_id
        required: true
        schema:
          description: ID of the API revision.
          examples:
          - 3f2b8c1e-7d4a-4e9b-a6c5-1d2e3f4a5b6c
          title: Revision Id
          type: string
      responses:
        '204':
          description: Successful Response
        '400':
          content:
            application/problem+json:
              example: *id169
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail'
          description: Bad Request
        '401':
